  <h2 id="routes">Mathematics career options: eight routes, led by real headroom</h2>

  <p>
    The routes are ordered by how far income and reach can grow, not by prestige or exam difficulty. Skill-led routes come first because you can sell the work and set the price. Rank-based and exam-led routes come last because pay is fixed and few people reach the top. The crowded and risky ones stay on the list, with the risk shown.
  </p>

