        <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>Growth move</span> {r.grow}</p>
        <p class="route-row route-row--violet"><span>First sales skill</span> {r.sell}</p>
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>

  <p>
    <strong>The boring 80%.</strong> Data work is mostly cleaning and checking. Actuarial work is documenting assumptions. Cryptography is implementing and testing. Optimisation is collecting messy inputs. Tutoring is preparation and follow-up. Research is reading and failed attempts. Ask which of these you can do happily for years.
  </p>

  <p>
    For the actuarial route, the exam pipeline, pass rates and pay by stage are covered in <a href="/blog/career-options/actuarial-science-careers/">actuarial science careers</a>. That guide is the place to test whether you can sustain years of papers.
  </p>

  <h2 id="two-stage">Routes that filter you twice</h2>

  <p>
    Some routes have a hard entry filter and then a separate hard filter later. A person can clear the first and still stall at the second, so plan for both.
  </p>

